  "project": "cube-3d",
  "description": "Plan 9.9 (X5.4, X5.4b) acceptance. A 0.15 m cube balanced on one corner by three body-axis reaction wheels, each mounted on the inside of the face opposite the pivot corner (wheel i centred on the face x_i = a, its centre d = 0.01 m inside it; wheel 0.08 kg, radius 0.055 m, thickness 0.012 m, axial inertia 1.9e-4, structure 0.18 kg): the plant is the hand-derived equation block library/CornerCube.jl (quaternion + body rates + relative wheel rates; total m = 0.42 kg, CoM (0.08738 m)(1,1,1), inertia about the pivot diag 8.278e-3 / off -3.1425e-3), driven by three ElectricDrive motors (R = 1 Ohm, L = 0.1 mH, k = 0.0335, rotor 1e-6) and a 2 ms discrete LQR (library/CubeLQR.jl, +-12 V) whose gain K (3 x 8) comes from design/design.py (finite-difference linearisation of an independent numpy replica, reduced state [tilt(2), omega(3), wheel(3)], DARE on (A/rho, B/rho), rho = 1.0005). Start: 2 degrees off the vertical. The reference numbers are design.py's non-linear closed loop (Radau, ZOH, clamp). DEC-M5-3: cube-3d-mb / cube-3d-mb-soft are the same cube built from the M3 spatial stdlib (Spherical3D pivot with kt = 1e8 / 1e6 N/m, RigidBody3D structure and wheels at their face positions, Revolute3D, ElectricDrive) under the same controller; the compare entries bound the difference by the pivot compliance and compare_scaling shows that the quasi-static part scales with 1/kt.",
